{%- doc -%}
  Declares the self-hosted heading face used by the DS Feature Banner.

  Emitted unconditionally: a browser only downloads a font file when some
  rule actually matches it, so this costs nothing while the section is
  using a face from Shopify's library instead.

  The file is deliberately absent from version control, so this resolves to
  a 404 on a checkout that has not had the licensed font added. That is
  harmless - the heading falls back to the generic serif in the stack.

  @example
  {% render 'ds-feature-banner-font' %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{% style %}
  @font-face {
    font-family: "Kessler Display";
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url({{ 'KesslerDisplay-Regular.otf' | asset_url }}) format("opentype");
  }
{% endstyle %}
